# Tauri 2

## Config

- Each program has `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` plus `src-tauri/tauri.windows.conf.json`. Keep them split.
- NSIS scripts live under `src-tauri/NSIS/` (e.g. `installer.nsh`). Do not add a second installer tree.
- Dev/package entrypoints: `src-tauri/scripts/dev.ts` and `src-tauri/scripts/package.ts`.

## Capabilities

- Allowlists live in `src-tauri/capabilities/` (`default`, `desktop`, `splashscreen`, `tray-menu`, `context-menus`).
- Capabilities JSON is the security boundary. Do not widen permissions to "make it work".
- Add a command to a capability only when that program needs it.

## IPC

- Frontend calls go through `packages/shell-bridge`. Do not scatter ad-hoc `invoke("...")` strings in program UI.
- Command names and payload types must match `crates/core` (and the Rust command). Do not invent a parallel API per program.
